+"""TPU-Friendly StreamIndex Top-K kernel -- VARIANT A, "Narrow Record".
+
+Step-3 variant of `measurement_and_design.md` section 3 (Option A). The ONLY
+change against `src/vllm_torchtpu/kernels/deepseek_v4/streamindex_topk.py` is
+the *format of the compressed-KV cache* and the reads that consume it. The
+arithmetic, the loop nest, the grid, the block sizes and the store are
+untouched, so this variant is bit-exact against the incumbent by construction.
+
+The format
+----------
+Incumbent, one array:
+
+    cache_kv  u8[num_pages, page_size//kv_packing, kv_packing, 256]
+              byte   0..127  the 128 fp8 (e4m3) key values
+              byte     128   the single e8m0 block scale
+              byte 129..255  padding -- never read, always transferred
+
+Variant, two arrays:
+
+    cache_val    u8[num_pages, page_size//kv_packing, kv_packing, 128]
+                 the 128 fp8 key values, and nothing else
+    cache_scale  u8[num_pages, page_size]
+                 the e8m0 scale for position `p` of page `g` at [g, p]
+
+129 used bytes per compressed position instead of 256, so the indexer read of
+this array falls by 49.6%. The scale plane is stored LANE-MAJOR (a whole page
+of 1024 scales along the minor axis) so that the in-VMEM `[bkv_sz, 1] -> [1,
+bkv_sz]` transpose the incumbent pays inside `load_bkv` disappears: the DMA
+lands the scales in exactly the layout `compute_scores` multiplies by.
+
+`cache_kv` is passed as a two-tuple `(cache_val, cache_scale)` so that the
+public signature -- and therefore the read-only instruments -- is unchanged.
+
+The writer side is NOT implemented here. Producing this format is a change to
+`mla_attention_op.py:103-104` and to the cache allocator; its cost is measured
+separately by `writer_probe.py` and reported as its own, un-netted number.
+"""
 
